<%# A single headline stat chip on the owner-only dashboard. Locals: label, value.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Hoojah 2026, Slice 2026 Phase 4.6) — mockup "Analytics · dashboard"
    ~lines 1466-1476. Two of these sit side by side with a 10px gap (`gap-3` on the row
    in `analytics/show`, not here — same "this partial owns no margin" rule `ui/_card`
    states for feed cards).

    RESTYLE from Slice 9 Task 4.7: the value moves off `text-primary` onto `text-ink`.
    That earlier choice made every stat chip read as a blue CTA-adjacent number; the
    mockup treats it as plain data typography — `var(--ink)`, the same token
    `shared/_screen_header`'s `<h1>` and every other headline number in the 2026
    redesign uses. The label moves `text-grey` → `text-ink-2`, the 2026 token for
    secondary/muted text (`app/assets/tailwind/application.css`), replacing the
    pre-2026 grey scale this partial hadn't been touched to migrate yet.

    Deliberately NO delta/percentage-change row. The mockup draws one ("↑ 12% this
    week") but nothing in this app computes a week-over-week comparison — `UserAnalytics`
    reads a live SUM off `hujahs`, not a snapshot, so there is no prior value to diff
    against. Inventing one would be fabricated data on a page whose entire premise is
    reading real, denormalized counters. If that number is ever wanted, it needs its own
    backing column/snapshot job first.

    Surface is `ui/_card`, `padded: true` for the `px-4 py-3` this file spelled by hand
    (see the note on `ui/_card`'s same-family padding trap for why `class:` never also
    carries padding).
%><%= render layout: "ui/card", locals: {padded: true, class: "flex-1 text-center"} do %>
  <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink"><%= value %></div>
  <div class="text-xs text-ink-2"><%= label %></div>
<% end %>
